# Even if in Russian: даже если, всё-таки, что бы ни
subtitle: "Say even if, still and whatever happens in Russian: да́же е́сли, всё-таки, хоть и, что бы ни, with из-за, благодаря́ and вме́сто, in Suzdal at minus twenty."
tags: ["russian","даже если","всё-таки","suzdal","russian grammar"]
teaches: ["grammar/concession","grammar/linking-words","grammar/prepositions"]
thumb: "band \"Even if it's minus twenty\" stamp \"STILL GOING\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"Building Russian words: решение, радость, помощник","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/147-russian-word-building.cast"}

## Even if in Russian: даже если, всё-таки, что бы ни
